  "details": "In StringLoading/ImageLoading, it appears that if the URL query contains URL-encoded characters (such as %41), the URL encoding for that query is skipped.\n\nFor example, a request to \"https://one.one.one.one?テスト\" succeeds, but a request to \"https://one.one.one.one?テスト%41\" fails.\n\nWhen checking the HTTP packets, I found that in the latter case, the query was sent as \"テストA\" without being encoded.\n\nSince this violates RFC 3986, Cloudflare responded with a 400 Bad Request.",
